# What this repo tracks: the Python source, and nothing else.
#
# Everything below is deliberately excluded. Note that .gitignore only affects
# UNTRACKED files -- anything already committed keeps being tracked until it is
# removed from the index with `git rm --cached`. That is why these rules looked
# like they were not working.

# --- real people's data. Never commit. -------------------------------------
# Raw rosters and teacher files carry student and teacher names, and the
# emitted timetable.json embeds teacher surnames in its lesson labels.
data/

# --- spreadsheets ----------------------------------------------------------
# Including Phase01_<year>.xlsx, which was tracked previously.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
~$*.xlsx

# --- documentation and notes ----------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md, README.md, docs/. See the note at the bottom of this file.
*.md
docs/

# --- tests and generated output -------------------------------------------
tests/
out/

# --- tooling and environments ---------------------------------------------
.claude/
.idea/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# NOTE: with *.md and docs/ excluded, the project's written record (CLAUDE.md,
# PLAN.md, PRODUCT.md) is NOT backed up by git. It exists only on this machine
# and in E:\timewiki. Back it up some other way, or drop the *.md rule.
